=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# firewall screen-lockout --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The Firewall screen. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13.$
# sshd on 2230, ufw active allowing 443 alone: a new SSH session$
# is refused. Item 1 lets it through.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Partial ssh blocked$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Refused$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Refused$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 443/tcp              Allow$
  [+] 443/tcp (v6)         Allow$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Let SSH through      Add its rules; other rules stay$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-3 or q]:$
$
$

